# Project Architecture

Expo (React Native) + TypeScript mobile apps using Expo Router for file-based routing.

## Directory Structure

- `app/` -- Expo Router routes (screens are thin wrappers)
- `src/components/` -- Feature components organized by domain (auth, investment, payments, etc.)
- `src/uikit/` -- Reusable UI components (core primitives + specialized components)
- `src/infra/` -- Infrastructure (fetch, interceptors, i18n, logger, tracking, analytics)
- `src/utils/` -- Utility functions (format, helpers, sharing, image)
- `src/assets/` -- Fonts, icons, images, locales, lottie animations
- `src/controllers/` -- Global controllers (popup management)

## Key Conventions

- Path alias: `@/*` maps to both root and `src/*`
- State: React Query (`useFetcher`) for server state, React Context for auth/config/pin
- i18n: i18next with `useTranslation()`, locale files in `src/assets/locales/`
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod, schema in separate `schema.ts` files
- Styling: Tailwind CSS via `className` prop (powered by `@colorye/react-native-css`)
- Navigation: `useRouter()` for navigation, `useLocalSearchParams()` for route params
- Commit convention: commitlint enforced via Husky pre-commit hooks
- Import sorting: alphabetized, no blank lines between groups (enforced by ESLint)
- No test files exist in this codebase currently
